# OPUS-ROOT-CALL-20260930-17: the two-argument form written above Other's declaration.  K03 (Codex -07 Q2, -08): a
# named Structure is a callable, visible throughout the unit in both directions, so Other below is the Structure here
# and Model exists: `Model: Other extra` is Model's call with two arguments -- an ordinary named Structure takes none
# -- refused where it stands.  (From OPUS-TYPED-BINDING-20260930-20 until K03 it was the typed binding of an absent
# Other; the typed binding `T: b c` itself waits for the author's question on model-constrained references.)
Model:
    size_t: value 1U
end: Model

int: extra 1
Model: Other extra

Other:
    size_t: p 2U
end: Other
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
